he presence of a person who either screamed themselves or scared the speaker. Choice D captures this element of surprise due to a hidden person being present.\n\nSince the audio sequence strongly supports the idea that the speaker's check for hidden people was immediately contradicted by a loud, startling event (the scream), D remains the most logical inference.\n\n**Conclusion:** The sequence of checking for hidden people, inviting entry, and then an immediate loud scream points to the surprise caused by an unexpected presence.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
